  q(EMER,'Chest pain caused by a temporary lack of oxygen to the heart muscle is called:','Angina pectoris',['Myocardial infarction','Hypertension','Syncope'],'B','Angina is usually relieved by rest and nitroglycerin, unlike a heart attack.',KD),
  q(EMER,'Death of part of the heart muscle due to a blocked blood supply is called:','Myocardial infarction',['Angina pectoris','Cerebrovascular accident','Arrhythmia'],'C','A myocardial infarction is a heart attack, and pain is usually not relieved by nitroglycerin.',KD),
  q(EMER,'A drop in blood pressure that causes dizziness when a patient stands up quickly is called:','Postural hypotension',['Hypertension','Hyperventilation','Hypoglycemia, or low blood sugar'],'D','Raising the dental chair slowly and having the patient sit for a moment helps prevent it.',KD),
  q(EMER,'Which drug is commonly used for a mild allergic reaction such as itching or hives?','Diphenhydramine',['Nitroglycerin','Epinephrine','Albuterol, which opens the airways during asthma'],'A','Diphenhydramine is an antihistamine; epinephrine is saved for severe reactions such as anaphylaxis.',KD),
  q(EMER,'Sudden swelling of the lips, tongue or face during an allergic reaction is called:','Angioedema',['Cellulitis','Hematoma','Emphysema, air trapped in the tissues'],'B','Angioedema can block the airway, so swelling of the tongue or throat is treated as an emergency.',KD),
  q(REST,'Which bridge has metal or ceramic wings bonded to the lingual surfaces of the neighboring teeth?','Maryland bridge',['Cantilever bridge','Full-coverage bridge','Implant-supported denture'],'C','A Maryland (resin-bonded) bridge needs little or no reduction of the neighboring teeth.',KD),
  q(REST,'In a fixed bridge, what is the natural tooth that supports the bridge called?','Abutment tooth',['Pontic','Connector','Coping, a thin metal cap'],'D','Abutment teeth are prepared for crowns, and the pontic is attached between them.',KD),
  q(REST,'A temporary crown worn while the final crown is being made is called a:','Provisional restoration',['Permanent crown','Veneer','Inlay'],'A','Provisional restorations protect the prepared tooth and keep neighboring teeth from shifting.',KD),
  q(REST,'Where a crown or filling meets the natural tooth structure is called the:','Margin',['Pontic','Cusp','Fissure'],'B','A smooth, well-sealed margin helps prevent recurrent decay and gum irritation.',KD),
  q(REST,'Which term describes a cut in the preparation that is wider at the base, helping lock an amalgam in place?','Undercut',['Bevel','Margin','Taper'],'C','Amalgam does not bond to the tooth, so undercuts give mechanical retention to the filling.',KD),
  q(HN,'What is the red part of the lips that meets the surrounding skin?','Vermilion border',['Philtrum','Commissure','Nasolabial fold'],'D','The vermilion border is checked during an oral cancer screening for changes in color or texture.',NEL),
  q(HN,'What is the vertical groove between the nose and the upper lip called?','Philtrum',['Commissure','Vermilion zone','Labial frenum, inside the lip'],'A','The philtrum forms where the facial processes join during development, which is linked to cleft lip.',NEL),
  q(HN,'Which cheek muscle helps keep food on the chewing surfaces of the teeth?','Buccinator',['Masseter','Temporalis','Orbicularis oris, around the lips'],'B','The buccinator forms the cheek wall and also helps with whistling and blowing.',NEL),
  q(HN,'Which is the smallest of the three major salivary glands?','Sublingual gland',['Parotid gland','Submandibular gland','Lacrimal gland, which makes tears'],'C','The sublingual gland lies under the tongue in the floor of the mouth and drains through several small ducts.',NEL),
  q(HN,'Which small pad of tissue lies behind the maxillary central incisors?','Incisive papilla',['Palatine rugae','Retromolar pad','Uvula'],'D','The incisive papilla covers the incisive foramen and is a landmark for the nasopalatine injection.',NEL),
  q(RAD,'Which X-ray setting controls the penetrating power of the beam?','Kilovoltage (kVp)',['Milliamperage (mA)','Exposure time','Collimation, which limits the beam size'],'A','Higher kVp produces X-rays with more energy, which lowers contrast and shows more shades of gray.',KD),
  q(RAD,'Which X-ray setting controls the number of X-rays produced?','Milliamperage (mA)',['Kilovoltage (kVp)','Filtration','Position indicator device length'],'B','Raising the mA makes more X-rays, which makes the image darker and increases density.',KD),
  q(RAD,'In labial mounting of radiographs, how should the raised dot face?','Toward the viewer',['Away from the viewer','Toward the floor','Toward the tongue side of the mount'],'C','Labial mounting shows the images as if the viewer is looking at the patient from the front.',KD),
  q(RAD,'In film processing, which solution removes unexposed crystals and hardens the film?','Fixer',['Developer','Water rinse','Replenisher, which tops up the solutions'],'D','The developer brings out the image, and the fixer clears unexposed crystals so the image is permanent.',KD),
  q(RAD,'A blurry duplicate image on the opposite side of a panoramic radiograph is called a:','Ghost image',['Cone cut','Herringbone pattern','Phantom limb'],'A','Ghost images come from metal objects such as earrings, so these are removed before a panoramic image.',KD),
  q(LAB,'In lost-wax casting, what is a sprue?','A channel that lets molten metal flow into the mold',['A type of impression tray','A gypsum model','A small brush'],'B','The sprue is attached to the wax pattern and leaves a channel when the wax is burned out.',KD),
  q(LAB,'Why is a wax spacer placed on a model before making a custom tray?','To leave room for the impression material',['To color the tray','To harden the acrylic','To glue the tray'],'C','The spacer creates an even space so the final impression material has a uniform thickness.',KD),
  q(LAB,'Which wax is wrapped around an impression to form walls before pouring a model?','Boxing wax',['Inlay wax','Bite registration wax','Sticky wax, used to join parts together'],'D','Boxing wax contains the poured stone and helps form a neat base for the model.',KD),
  q(LAB,'Which machine with spinning wheels is used to polish dentures in the lab?','Dental lathe',['Model trimmer','Vibrator','Articulator, which simulates jaw movements'],'A','A lathe with pumice and polishing wheels gives dentures and acrylic appliances a smooth, shiny surface.',KD),
  q(LAB,'What happens when too much water is used when mixing gypsum?','The cast is weaker',['The cast is stronger','The mix sets instantly','The cast becomes harder and shinier than normal'],'B','Extra water leaves more space between crystals, so the set gypsum is weaker and less hard.',KD)
